{"The change removes the max(0, offset) clamping when cursor.is_prev is true, allowing user-controlled negative offsets to reach Django's queryset slicing which raises an unhandled AssertionError. Any authenticated user can crash any endpoint using BasePaginator/DateTimePaginator by sending a cursor like 0:-5:1.": 0.9653537273406982, "OrganizationAuditLogsEndpoint can switch to OptimizedCursorPaginator while ordering by '-datetime', but OptimizedCursorPaginator.get_item_key applies math.floor/math.ceil to the field value. With a datetime field (AuditLogEntry.datetime), this will raise a TypeError during pagination and break the endpoint when optimized_pagination=true is used by an eligible admin.": 0.9865198135375977, "The gate organization_context.member.has_global_access is True by default for all organization members because the DB model defines has_global_access = models.BooleanField(default=True). The or condition means any org member can activate the OptimizedCursorPaginator path by passing ?optimized_pagination=true, completely defeating the intended admin-only restriction.": 0.5570155382156372, "The variable organization_context is used but never defined in the method scope, resulting in a NameError crash. This completely breaks the endpoint when users attempt to check for advanced pagination permissions.": 0.4654916524887085}